When this marker is present, every L1-flagged MCP tool's Zod input schema
declares `workspace: z.string().min(1)` (or equivalent required form). The
schema-layer Zod validation surfaces missing-workspace as an input-validation
error; handlers also defend-in-depth with a workspace_required envelope to
match the REST 400 shape for callers that bypass the SDK's strip.
